 "response": "Tepi's budget is now **$2246K**.\n\n**How I worked it out**\n\n1. **Who counts:** Only Finance Office budget entries change the figure. Messages from Sales, Legal, Operations, PMO, Vendor, Facilities, Engineering and Marketing are ignored. So are Finance Office notes that don't change the budget, such as audits, receipts and room changes.\n\n2. **Withdrawal chains:** Each chain was resolved from its latest link backward. A withdrawal counts only if no later, still-valid withdrawal cancels it. Some examples:\n   - **#0002:** #0005 withdraws #0002, and #0018 withdraws #0005. Then #0031 withdraws #0018, #0504 withdraws #0031, and #1545 withdraws #0504. With #0504 cancelled, #0031 stands, which cancels #0018. That leaves #0005 in force, so #0002 stays withdrawn.\n   - **#0035:** The chain runs #0069 \u2192 #0078 \u2192 #0084 \u2192 #0110 \u2192 #0119 \u2192 #0176 \u2192 #0331 \u2192 #0920. #0920 stands, which leaves #0069's withdrawal cancelled. So #0035's +$593K still applies.\n   - **#0011:** #0038 withdraws it, but #0525 withdraws #0038. So the +$208K applies.\n\n   In total, 112 budget updates end up withdrawn and are skipped.\n\n3. **Running total:** Starting from $1810K (#0001), I applied every remaining Finance Office increase and decrease in record order. The last one is #1596 (\u2212$15K), which brings the total from $2261K to $2246K.\n\nANSWER: $2246K",
